    "body": "Dear Data Protection Officer,\n\nI am writing to raise a concern about the privacy information provided on https://talldwarfhosting.com/.\n\nOur review was based on an automated, passive audit using a fresh browser session. We checked the site and reviewed the privacy policy available at https://talldwarfhosting.com/TallDwarf%20Privacy%20Policy.pdf.\n\nDuring this audit, we did not find a cookie banner on the website.\n\nIn addition, our automated review suggests that the privacy policy may be missing some information required under UK GDPR Article 13(1)-(2). In particular, the policy we reviewed does not appear to cover:\n\n1. How long personal data is kept.\n2. The right to complain to the Information Commissioner\u2019s Office.\n\nPlease would you:\n\n1. Explain each of the points above.\n2. Confirm which cookies or trackers you consider strictly necessary or otherwise exempt, and why.\n3. Stop any non-essential tracking without consent, if any such tracking is taking place.\n4. Reply within one month.\n\nIf this matter is not resolved, it may be raised with the Information Commissioner\u2019s Office.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\nJoshua Baker",
